# Typed Python

All **new and changed** Python must be fully typed. Prefer gradual typing only when fixing legacy call sites in the same change.

## Do

- Annotate parameters, return types, and non-obvious locals on public functions/methods
- Use `list[T]`, `dict[K, V]`, `|` unions, and `TypedDict` / pydantic models where they fit
- Run `just typecheck` (or the project’s `uv run ty check`) before finishing Python work

## Don't

- Leave public APIs unannotated
- Use bare `Any` to silence the checker without a short comment explaining why
- Skip `ty` failures and rely on runtime-only discovery
